00:02:37.725 --> 00:02:37.791
Today's Special Feature:

00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:37.992
Today's Special Feature:
It's the Detective Prince, Naoto Shirogane!

00:02:37.992 --> 00:02:41.095
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince
It's the Detective Prince, Naoto Shirogane!

00:02:41.095 --> 00:02:41.595
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:42.897
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince
Thank you for having me.

00:02:42.897 --> 00:02:43.430
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:48.936
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince
So then, is it true this mystery-laden case
is finally closed?

00:02:48.936 --> 00:02:49.103
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince

00:02:49.103 --> 00:02:50.171
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince
It's not.

00:02:50.171 --> 00:02:50.237
Today's Special Feature:
The High School Student and Detective Prince

00:02:50.237 --> 00:02:51.205
When viewing the case as a whole,
I fail to reach the same conclusion as the police.

00:02:51.205 --> 00:02:55.409
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders
When viewing the case as a whole,
I fail to reach the same conclusion as the police.

00:02:56.143 --> 00:02:58.373
Wh-what do you mean?

00:02:58.579 --> 00:02:58.979
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders

00:02:58.979 --> 00:03:03.918
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders
I cannot make a concrete statement yet,
but something feels off.

00:03:04.084 --> 00:03:06.985
Uh, well, um... Shirogane?

00:03:07.721 --> 00:03:08.589
Huh?

00:03:08.589 --> 00:03:08.822
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders
Huh?

00:03:08.822 --> 00:03:08.889
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders

00:03:08.889 --> 00:03:10.758
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders
I met him at the festival.

00:03:10.758 --> 00:03:10.891
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders

00:03:10.891 --> 00:03:13.160
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders
There were three victims in this case.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:13.227
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders

00:03:13.227 --> 00:03:16.931
High School Student and Detective Prince
Searching for the Truth About the Murders
I believe we should pursue
even the slightest inconsistencies.

00:03:27.341 --> 00:03:29.910
I was kinda surprised.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.111
By what?

00:03:31.111 --> 00:03:32.043
Naoto!

00:03:32.346 --> 00:03:34.415
The distinguished Detective Prince?

00:03:34.415 --> 00:03:36.884
Oh, you mean that program last night?

00:03:36.884 --> 00:03:42.413
Yeah. I didn't think he was the type
that would want to go on TV.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:45.625
Indeed, I prefer to not go on TV.

00:03:46.493 --> 00:03:47.755
Naoto!

00:03:49.363 --> 00:03:50.762
Do you have a moment?

00:03:51.065 --> 00:03:52.499
Just Like Mama's Cooking
SOUFAL DALGAKU

00:03:52.499 --> 00:03:53.634
Just Like Mama's Cooking
SOUFAL DALGAKU
Here! Come again.

00:03:55.269 --> 00:04:00.332
I was hoping to disclose my current
thoughts on the case with you.

00:04:01.675 --> 00:04:05.111
Hey, now! The case is closed already.

00:04:05.779 --> 00:04:07.872
Didn't you say something felt wrong?

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:11.944
Right. First, there are the
commonalities between the victims.

00:04:12.553 --> 00:04:15.989
They were always kidnapped
before they were murdered.

00:04:16.357 --> 00:04:22.318
They were locals who'd suddenly obtained fame
through a certain degree of media attention.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:27.824
In any case, I believe the victims' personal traits
were of minimal importance.

00:04:28.502 --> 00:04:33.235
There are several of you
who fit this profile, aren't there?

00:04:34.575 --> 00:04:36.873
How do you figure that?

00:04:37.845 --> 00:04:41.645
There was a lengthy gap
between the second and third murders.

00:04:42.116 --> 00:04:46.576
But there wasn't a gap between the number of
disappearances that fit these criteria.

00:04:47.021 --> 00:04:48.181
Yukiko Amagi,

00:04:48.422 --> 00:04:49.821
Kanji Tatsumi,

00:04:50.057 --> 00:04:51.422
Rise Kujikawa...

00:04:52.092 --> 00:04:55.462
All three of you went missing
after you were featured on TV.

00:04:55.462 --> 00:04:58.431
But somehow you managed to survive.

00:04:59.867 --> 00:05:05.773
Or perhaps you disguised yourselves
as victims to avert police suspicion.

00:05:05.773 --> 00:05:07.638
What are you getting at?!

00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:13.647
Some of you were in contact with the victims,
so perhaps one of you was...

00:05:13.647 --> 00:05:16.083
Whoa, hold it! You-

00:05:16.083 --> 00:05:16.879
Yosuke!

00:05:18.152 --> 00:05:20.950
Hey, look! Isn't that the Detective Prince?

00:05:23.424 --> 00:05:25.289
Let's take this elsewhere.

00:05:28.962 --> 00:05:34.093
So you think that one of us was the killer?

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:40.163
I considered that possibility,
but now I believe the exact opposite.

00:05:40.607 --> 00:05:41.699
How so?

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.879
You weren't the killers,

00:05:45.879 --> 00:05:49.781
but rather people somehow able
to go after the culprit.

00:05:52.986 --> 00:05:56.649
You obtain a new ally
each time you rescue someone.

00:05:57.191 --> 00:06:00.922
If I look at it from that angle,
all of the dots connect.

00:06:01.795 --> 00:06:03.626
But if that's the case,

00:06:03.731 --> 00:06:06.495
then something isn't right
with Mr. Morooka's murder.

00:06:07.101 --> 00:06:10.604
He didn't get media attention
nor did he go missing.

00:06:10.604 --> 00:06:13.334
Above all else, there was an
inconsistency with his corpse.

00:06:13.507 --> 00:06:14.633
How so?

00:06:14.742 --> 00:06:18.735
He was hung upside-down
just like Miss Yamano and Konishi!

00:06:20.114 --> 00:06:23.016
True, he was found in a similar position.

00:06:23.016 --> 00:06:27.588
We are unable to identify the
cause of death for the prior two cases,

00:06:27.588 --> 00:06:31.752
but we discerned that Mr. Morooka
died from a strong blow to the head.

00:06:32.159 --> 00:06:36.730
The police are unable to satisfactorily
resolve this issue,

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.324
but they are desperate to close the case.

00:06:39.967 --> 00:06:40.695
So?

00:06:44.271 --> 00:06:50.077
As a result, action must be taken to obtain...

00:06:50.077 --> 00:06:51.374
...conclusive evidence.

00:06:56.216 --> 00:06:57.877
How will this pan out?

00:06:58.852 --> 00:07:01.252
H-hey, where are you going?

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:07.224
During our school trip, you mentioned
something rather intriguing.

00:07:08.862 --> 00:07:13.322
"We go into the TV to rescue people
after they get kidnapped."

00:07:13.667 --> 00:07:15.430
Oh, well...

00:07:15.736 --> 00:07:19.069
I don't think of this as a game.

00:07:34.988 --> 00:07:39.126
Wasn't that Naoto on
Midnight Channel last night?

00:07:39.126 --> 00:07:41.094
It definitely resembled him...

00:07:41.628 --> 00:07:45.724
I asked Kuma and he said
no one's on the other side.

00:07:46.066 --> 00:07:49.092
But didn't we already catch the killer?

00:07:49.937 --> 00:07:54.704
If the case is closed, why did he
show up on Midnight Channel?

00:07:55.409 --> 00:08:00.403
Ultimately, what the heck is
Midnight Channel anyway?

00:08:12.092 --> 00:08:13.616
Good evening, everyone.

00:08:13.727 --> 00:08:16.525
I am the Detective Prince, Naoto Shirogane.

00:08:17.231 --> 00:08:20.723
Welcome to the Experiment of the Century:
The Genome Project.

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:24.292
I shall hereby undergo
a body-altering operation.

00:08:25.005 --> 00:08:26.131
A what?

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.470
I will use a glorious yet
forbidden secret method!

00:08:31.378 --> 00:08:36.816
Everyone will get to see
as I embark on my new journey.

00:08:37.451 --> 00:08:39.419
Watch as I am born anew!

00:08:41.755 --> 00:08:46.852
It will be the day I start walking down
a completely different path in life.

00:08:47.327 --> 00:08:51.593
I would like to share this
commemorative day with all of you.

00:08:52.032 --> 00:08:53.932
Be sure to tune in.

00:09:01.842 --> 00:09:02.309
Hel-

00:09:02.309 --> 00:09:05.445
Senpai! I-I just saw N-Naoto crystal-clear!

00:09:05.445 --> 00:09:06.213
Calm-
Senpai! I-I just saw N-Naoto crystal-clear!

00:09:06.213 --> 00:09:09.341
What's going on?! Didn't we catch the killer?!

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:12.815
This proves that Naoto's gut feeling was right.

00:09:13.053 --> 00:09:16.318
What good's that if he gets himself kidnapped?!

00:09:16.924 --> 00:09:19.620
Damn, he pisses me off!

00:09:20.027 --> 00:09:21.595
Want me to gather the group?

00:09:21.595 --> 00:09:22.429
Please.

00:09:22.429 --> 00:09:23.555
Got it!

00:09:32.105 --> 00:09:32.935
Sniff, sniff!

00:09:33.507 --> 00:09:36.209
There's definitely someone in here.

00:09:36.209 --> 00:09:39.440
And... this world is growing larger.

00:09:39.713 --> 00:09:42.015
Way to go, Rise!

00:09:42.015 --> 00:09:44.351
My snout's burnt out.

00:09:44.351 --> 00:09:46.587
Want me to rub your shoulders?

00:09:46.587 --> 00:09:47.645
Don't distract her!

00:09:48.488 --> 00:09:51.758
What's going on?
Does this mean the case isn't over?

00:09:51.758 --> 00:09:54.328
So it's still going on like before...

00:09:54.328 --> 00:09:56.455
It's the same...

00:09:56.663 --> 00:10:01.268
I see! That's why Naoto
suddenly decided to go on TV.

00:10:01.268 --> 00:10:05.762
I bet you're right. Only locals who were
aired on TV have been kidnapped.

00:10:06.206 --> 00:10:08.008
He made himself bait?

00:10:08.008 --> 00:10:10.844
He wouldn't! He could get killed!

00:10:10.844 --> 00:10:14.974
That moron! The least
he coulda done was warn us!

00:10:15.782 --> 00:10:18.615
He said this wasn't a game.

00:10:20.354 --> 00:10:21.722
What should I do?

00:10:21.722 --> 00:10:24.282
It's my fault. Because of what I said...

00:10:25.025 --> 00:10:26.014
Rise...

00:10:26.126 --> 00:10:29.796
It's no use. I can tell he's here,
but I can't find him.

00:10:29.796 --> 00:10:32.966
It's too dangerous to wander around blindly.

00:10:32.966 --> 00:10:34.797
We'd become lost li'I cubs!

00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:36.196
Damn it!

00:10:36.837 --> 00:10:39.237
It can't be helped. Let's leave for now.

00:10:41.108 --> 00:10:45.278
So, if the case isn't over,
what's the deal with Kubo?

00:10:45.278 --> 00:10:47.614
Didn't he kill King Moron?

00:10:47.614 --> 00:10:49.683
Remember what Naoto said?

00:10:49.683 --> 00:10:53.312
It's weird how they could only identify
Mr. Morooka's cause of death.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:58.191
Right. And he's the only one
who never entered the TV.

00:10:58.191 --> 00:11:01.528
The killer didn't change his methods
with King Moron.

00:11:01.528 --> 00:11:04.053
It was a different killer to begin with.

00:11:04.464 --> 00:11:07.661
So the person who kidnapped Naoto
is the real culprit?

00:11:08.001 --> 00:11:12.005
But Kubo confessed that he
killed the others, remember?

00:11:12.005 --> 00:11:16.243
So he took the rap for someone else?
Isn't that weird?

00:11:16.243 --> 00:11:20.111
And there's something else bugging me. It's uh...

00:11:20.514 --> 00:11:23.381
Who cares about someone behind bars?

00:11:23.784 --> 00:11:26.586
If we don't hurry, that idiot's gonna croak!

00:11:26.586 --> 00:11:32.192
Sorry, but I need more information
so I can get a better picture of him.

00:11:32.192 --> 00:11:34.261
More info, huh?

00:11:34.261 --> 00:11:37.594
Damn it! We don't know shit about him!

00:11:38.465 --> 00:11:40.865
Let's split up and gather information on Naoto.

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:50.410
I don't know if this is related to Naoto or not,
but hasn't the town seemed weird of late?

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:51.611
It's weird?

00:11:51.611 --> 00:11:54.247
Everyone seems strangely happy...

00:11:54.247 --> 00:11:56.750
They're always talking about others.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.786
That's nothing new, you know?

00:11:59.786 --> 00:12:03.654
Isn't it their way of showing
they're relieved that icky case is closed?

00:12:04.458 --> 00:12:08.121
But still, it doesn't feel right...

00:12:08.862 --> 00:12:12.161
It's like they're afraid of something.

00:12:15.435 --> 00:12:17.665
Courage:
Daring
Knowledge: Diligence:
Expert Staunch
Expression: Understanding:
Touching Motherly

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.670
Courage:
Daring
Knowledge: Diligence:
Expert Staunch
Expression: Understanding:
Touching Motherly

00:12:28.615 --> 00:12:30.050
The Detective Prince?

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:33.754
Oh, doesn't he have like seven secretaries?

00:12:33.754 --> 00:12:35.789
It's so cool he gets a different one every day!

00:12:35.789 --> 00:12:36.256
Isn't it?

00:12:36.256 --> 00:12:36.757
Care to pick me up and make me
your secretary each day of the week?
Isn't it?

00:12:36.757 --> 00:12:40.488
Care to pick me up and make me
your secretary each day of the week?

00:12:40.694 --> 00:12:42.025
Shuddup!

00:12:42.329 --> 00:12:43.318
T-thanks...

00:12:43.396 --> 00:12:44.998
He was awful!

00:12:44.998 --> 00:12:45.899
Talk about gross.

00:12:45.899 --> 00:12:48.163
She's remarrying again!

00:12:48.401 --> 00:12:49.868
Okay, got it.

00:12:51.304 --> 00:12:54.637
Satonaka hasn't had any luck yet either.

00:12:54.841 --> 00:13:00.580
Shit! This town's friggin' puny,
so why can't we find any useful info?!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.946
He stands out like a sore thumb!

00:13:06.353 --> 00:13:08.688
Hello. I'm busy right-

00:13:08.688 --> 00:13:09.890
What?!

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:10.857
What is it?

00:13:11.525 --> 00:13:14.585
My Old Lady got taken to the hospital!

00:13:14.928 --> 00:13:16.096
Inaba Municipal
Hospital

00:13:16.096 --> 00:13:17.130
Inaba Municipal
Hospital
What?!

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:17.494
What?!

00:13:17.597 --> 00:13:20.361
You brought someone here,
not the other way 'round?!

00:13:20.934 --> 00:13:24.237
Shhh! Don't shout in a hospital.

00:13:24.237 --> 00:13:26.139
B-but...

00:13:26.139 --> 00:13:31.711
I saw the poor boy get hit by a bicycle
right in front of me.

00:13:31.711 --> 00:13:35.515
Since he hit his head,
I wanted him to see a doctor.

00:13:35.515 --> 00:13:38.814
But they said he's fine. Isn't that wonderful?

00:13:39.019 --> 00:13:40.213
Cut the crap!

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.720
You're shouting again.

00:13:44.024 --> 00:13:44.991
Damn it!

00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:49.989
I'm fine! I won't go down without a fight.

00:13:50.197 --> 00:13:52.332
It's not like you to worry.

00:13:52.332 --> 00:13:54.163
Shut up, ya old hag!

00:13:54.601 --> 00:13:55.669
Oh, yes.

00:13:55.669 --> 00:14:01.630
Those stuffed animals you made
to aid store profits are quite popular.

00:14:02.075 --> 00:14:03.235
Thank you.

00:14:04.778 --> 00:14:08.009
They're knitted animals, not stuffed animals.

00:14:08.682 --> 00:14:11.082
I swear, everyone's driving me nuts.

00:14:18.191 --> 00:14:19.626
Aiya

00:14:19.626 --> 00:14:21.361
Sorry 'bout that.

00:14:21.361 --> 00:14:23.363
I'm glad it wasn't anything serious.

00:14:23.363 --> 00:14:26.958
Let's make up for lost time after we eat.

00:14:27.467 --> 00:14:32.405
Dammit! Pullin' stunts, never considering
how others might feel!

00:14:32.405 --> 00:14:35.508
Do you mean your mom or Naoto?

00:14:35.508 --> 00:14:38.341
Huh? Well, both.

00:14:39.079 --> 00:14:40.740
Here's your nikudon.

00:14:42.082 --> 00:14:43.250
Thanks.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:44.851
Oh, right.

00:14:44.851 --> 00:14:49.379
Since you go around town makin' deliveries,
have you heard anything about Naoto?

00:14:49.856 --> 00:14:53.493
The Detective Prince... got in a fight.

00:14:53.493 --> 00:14:54.628
A fight?!

00:14:54.628 --> 00:14:55.560
Who with?

00:14:55.996 --> 00:14:58.191
He was arguing with an officer?

00:14:58.498 --> 00:14:59.556
Why?

00:15:00.233 --> 00:15:03.870
Supposedly he frequently criticized
how they were handling the case.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:08.898
At any rate, Naoto's obsession
with the case seems abnormal.

00:15:09.309 --> 00:15:11.675
I wonder why he was so fixated on it.

00:15:12.445 --> 00:15:17.678
The way the police treated him like a kid
might have something to do with it.

00:15:17.884 --> 00:15:20.682
Aika knew all that?

00:15:21.154 --> 00:15:25.420
No, she only told us that he was
fighting with an officer.

00:15:25.659 --> 00:15:27.957
You know? That lame cop.

00:15:28.929 --> 00:15:31.056
Oh, Adachi!

00:15:31.464 --> 00:15:34.763
I see... So he's super stubborn.

00:15:35.335 --> 00:15:37.701
And he's surprisingly emotional.

00:15:39.005 --> 00:15:41.132
I'm getting a picture of him.

00:15:47.447 --> 00:15:50.016
What is this place?

00:15:50.016 --> 00:15:52.712
Doesn't it look like a secret base
from an action show?

00:15:53.653 --> 00:15:56.781
I've heard filming those is tough.

00:15:56.990 --> 00:16:00.255
It's all dusty and hot as hell
with the bright lights.

00:16:02.862 --> 00:16:04.130
What's wrong?

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:10.036
Kuma, aren't the buildings and events in this
world made from people's repressed emotions?

00:16:10.036 --> 00:16:11.230
Yes!

00:16:12.038 --> 00:16:15.906
Do you remember what Naoto said
on Midnight Channel?

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:22.642
It will be the day I start walking down
a completely different path in life.

00:16:23.984 --> 00:16:27.921
I thought Naoto was rejecting his life
as a boy detective.

00:16:27.921 --> 00:16:29.548
So what of it?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.489
This secret lab.

00:16:32.292 --> 00:16:36.429
It looks like one of those old sets where
boy detectives or heroes solve cases.

00:16:36.429 --> 00:16:37.864
You have a point.

00:16:37.864 --> 00:16:44.269
But if this came from Naoto's mind,
he's got a kinda cute side to him.

00:16:45.805 --> 00:16:49.172
I dunno 'bout none of that,
but I do know one thing.

00:16:49.576 --> 00:16:50.975
What's that?

00:16:52.312 --> 00:16:55.941
He's running away from something too.

00:16:57.317 --> 00:16:59.919
Warning! Intruders!

00:16:59.919 --> 00:17:02.217
Wow! Looks like you're right.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:05.058
Naoto!

00:17:05.058 --> 00:17:08.595
Oh, I was getting tired of waiting.

00:17:08.595 --> 00:17:11.931
I've just about had it with this child.

00:17:11.931 --> 00:17:14.934
No, no, no! Don't go!

00:17:14.934 --> 00:17:16.970
That's Naoto's Shadow?

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.961
It looks like a little kid!

00:17:20.206 --> 00:17:21.605
Senpai, look up!

00:17:24.711 --> 00:17:26.611
They're below us, too!

00:17:31.918 --> 00:17:33.044
Here they come!

00:17:33.953 --> 00:17:37.354
Speaking with you is meaningless. I'm leaving.

00:17:37.891 --> 00:17:38.983
Why?

00:17:39.092 --> 00:17:41.060
Why do I always get left behind?

00:17:41.161 --> 00:17:43.493
Why am I always left all alone?

00:17:43.997 --> 00:17:46.488
I'm lonely... So lonely!

00:17:47.734 --> 00:17:49.361
We share the same face...

00:17:49.869 --> 00:17:52.770
It's as if you are trying to say that you are me.

00:17:53.206 --> 00:17:58.644
But as long as you act like a child,
we are nothing alike.

00:18:00.713 --> 00:18:02.908
Who are you trying to fool?

00:18:03.016 --> 00:18:04.745
You know the truth, don't you?

00:18:06.119 --> 00:18:08.519
I am you!

00:18:15.562 --> 00:18:16.426
BURNING
UP!

00:18:17.297 --> 00:18:18.491
Persona!

00:18:29.976 --> 00:18:32.410
I am not "acting" like a child.

00:18:32.645 --> 00:18:34.044
This is the true you.

00:18:34.414 --> 00:18:36.177
Naoto, don't argue with him!

00:18:36.516 --> 00:18:37.346
No!

00:18:39.319 --> 00:18:41.150
He has to face this.

00:18:42.789 --> 00:18:44.086
Haven't we...

00:18:46.092 --> 00:18:48.185
...all had to go through this?

00:18:49.395 --> 00:18:51.556
Remember what everyone says?

00:18:51.664 --> 00:18:54.963
"You're just a kid! Just a measly kid!"

00:19:01.941 --> 00:19:05.468
People only want your brains.

00:19:06.045 --> 00:19:09.481
Once they're done with you,
they send you back home.

00:19:11.251 --> 00:19:14.982
There's nothing you can do about
the world's dual expectations.

00:19:15.722 --> 00:19:17.747
You're a lonely child.

00:19:18.324 --> 00:19:21.259
I want to become a man right now.

00:19:21.594 --> 00:19:24.119
I want people to see me for who I am!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:27.427
I want a reason to exist!

00:19:30.036 --> 00:19:30.934
Stop it...

00:19:31.337 --> 00:19:34.431
I can determine my own reason for existence!

00:19:35.208 --> 00:19:39.076
You can't! How will you change the fact
that you are currently a child?

00:19:41.014 --> 00:19:42.382
Stop it...

00:19:42.382 --> 00:19:49.083
Don't you admire those cool,
strong men in detective novels?

00:19:49.322 --> 00:19:54.658
If you flip it around, it's proof that you
consider yourself a child deep down.

00:19:54.761 --> 00:19:55.962
You're lying!

00:19:55.962 --> 00:20:00.626
Naoto Shirogane...
Isn't it a cool, masculine name?

00:20:01.467 --> 00:20:02.435
But...

00:20:02.435 --> 00:20:03.094
Don't!

00:20:03.403 --> 00:20:05.471
You can't change the truth.

00:20:05.471 --> 00:20:06.597
Stop it!

00:20:07.173 --> 00:20:10.904
You can't overcome the gender barrier.

00:20:11.711 --> 00:20:14.111
You aren't even a guy!

00:20:14.581 --> 00:20:18.176
You could never become
a strong man someday!

00:20:18.484 --> 00:20:19.109
Eh?!

00:20:19.485 --> 00:20:20.353
Eh?!

00:20:20.353 --> 00:20:23.322
Whoa, I can't believe my ears!

00:20:24.123 --> 00:20:26.318
You aren't a... dude?

00:20:26.659 --> 00:20:29.229
I don't intend to whine about it.

00:20:29.229 --> 00:20:31.264
That wouldn't resolve anything.

00:20:31.264 --> 00:20:34.290
You've had people
tell you that a lot, haven't you?

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:38.734
"Whining won't resolve anything, Naoto."

00:20:39.906 --> 00:20:41.635
Didn't that make you cry?

00:20:41.741 --> 00:20:43.709
And here you are saying that same thing.

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:45.835
What are you trying to protect?

00:20:47.614 --> 00:20:49.605
You don't have to push so hard anymore...

00:20:49.716 --> 00:20:52.276
I know exactly how you feel.

00:20:52.385 --> 00:20:54.420
After all, I am you...

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:55.478
No!

00:20:55.688 --> 00:20:56.856
Don't do it!

00:20:56.856 --> 00:20:59.290
No, let her get it out.

00:20:59.492 --> 00:21:00.356
Kanji!

00:21:01.828 --> 00:21:04.854
Otherwise, she'll continue to suffer!

00:21:05.598 --> 00:21:08.624
You... You aren't me!

00:21:17.143 --> 00:21:18.542
We...

00:21:19.245 --> 00:21:22.772
I am a Shadow, the true self.

00:21:23.683 --> 00:21:25.947
We just gotta do our thing...

00:21:26.085 --> 00:21:28.110
...and kick some serious ass!

00:21:28.221 --> 00:21:30.519
How dare you act so almighty!

00:21:31.291 --> 00:21:36.752
I loathe violent guys who let their
emotions get the best of them!

00:21:38.564 --> 00:21:42.364
Come on! It's body-altering time!

00:21:46.139 --> 00:21:47.163
No!

00:21:49.976 --> 00:21:51.204
Stop it!

00:21:52.078 --> 00:21:52.976
Let's do it!

00:21:53.179 --> 00:21:54.043
Yeah!

00:21:54.714 --> 00:21:58.115
What? More people sick with their lives?

00:21:58.251 --> 00:22:01.448
I'll just have to give you a special operation!

00:22:08.027 --> 00:22:09.085
Yosuke!

00:22:11.397 --> 00:22:15.168
Did she modify my body?

00:22:15.168 --> 00:22:17.261
No, this isn't a modification.

00:22:17.704 --> 00:22:19.467
She didn't modify you, but...

00:22:19.972 --> 00:22:20.940
...she aged you!

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:22.407
She what?!

00:22:22.842 --> 00:22:23.910
You serious?!

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:25.400
Oh, Yo-Yo-Yosuke!

00:22:25.678 --> 00:22:27.447
T-those wrinkles!

00:22:27.447 --> 00:22:28.414
His teeth!

00:22:28.414 --> 00:22:29.540
Liver spots!

00:22:29.782 --> 00:22:32.774
Now for the operation!

00:22:33.186 --> 00:22:34.517
No!

00:22:38.224 --> 00:22:39.782
No!

00:23:04.384 --> 00:23:11.691
I look at the rustic scenery

00:23:11.691 --> 00:23:17.864
Along the path to school we walked together

00:23:17.864 --> 00:23:22.335
Campus at spring

00:23:22.335 --> 00:23:26.172
The flood plane the summer festival

00:23:26.172 --> 00:23:30.276
These were the days we spent

00:23:30.276 --> 00:23:38.342
shoulder-to-shoulder laughing together

00:23:38.684 --> 00:23:47.393
From past to present

00:23:47.393 --> 00:23:55.198
I've always looked back on these carefree days

00:23:55.435 --> 00:23:59.439
From today to tomorrow

00:23:59.439 --> 00:24:03.273
And from tomorrow to the future

00:24:04.811 --> 00:24:11.384
We move forward while treasuring

00:24:11.384 --> 00:24:16.287
The bonds we've made

00:24:18.424 --> 00:24:20.560
Let me alter your bodies already!

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:21.494
Narukami!

00:24:21.494 --> 00:24:23.196
You've been so good to me...

00:24:23.196 --> 00:24:24.497
She's one crazy lady.

00:24:24.497 --> 00:24:26.065
Don't forget about me!

00:24:26.065 --> 00:24:27.934
No one needs me anymore...

00:24:27.934 --> 00:24:28.935
Everyone, run for it!

00:24:28.935 --> 00:24:30.903
I feel full of life!
